    intro="Epics vs stories vs tasks is a question about size and purpose: an epic is a large goal that spans several Sprints, a user story is a small slice of value for a user that fits in one Sprint, and a task is a technical step the team takes to finish a story. Together they turn a broad objective into work people can pick up today. This guide compares the three levels, shows a full worked example, explains how Jira and other tools name them, and gives you a step-by-step way to break work down.",
